{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals","id":3710,"title":"Explain, please: Asna Firstborn, the Loom and Sidereals.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-05T13:06:37-08:00","id":3710,"title":"Explain, please: Asna Firstborn, the Loom and Sidereals.","content":"I have a question about Asna Firstborn's power over the Loom. Is she capable to cut off a Sidereal from the Loom and deprive him/her of most of the their Exaltions tricks, charms and astrology? Or will a Sidereal blast away any such attempt with anti-shaping defences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/784-durabys","user":"Durabys","date":". 09-07-2014, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/784-durabys","name":"Durabys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T13:47:16-08:00","id":3726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Durabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals#post3710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about Asna Firstborn's power over the Loom. Is she capable to cut off a Sidereal from the Loom and deprive him/hem of most of the their Exaltions tricks, charms and astrology? Or will a Sidereal blast away any such attempt with anti-shaping defences?</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory, nothing can prevent a Sidereal's powers from functioning, not even his Astrology, until/unless he's accumulated enough Paradox. Charms always work, and not even the Maidens can take back access to Charms once granted.<br /> <br /> That said, I could see Asna and her children causing some trouble with Astrology, if they happen to not like the guy. Charms always work, though; those are inherent in the character, regardless of how they're supposed to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T13:54:28-08:00","id":3732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Durabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals#post3710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about Asna Firstborn's power over the Loom. Is she capable to cut off a Sidereal from the Loom and deprive him/hem of most of the their Exaltions tricks, charms and astrology? Or will a Sidereal blast away any such attempt with anti-shaping defences?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking in generalities, you probably won't see an entity who has &quot;flip off all of an Exalted's cool stuff by remote control&quot; among their powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T14:02:22-08:00","id":3736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=3732#post3732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking in generalities, you probably won't see an entity who has &quot;flip off all of an Exalted's cool stuff by remote control&quot; among their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chiefly among the in-setting reasons being &quot;they'd be chumps in the PW otherwise&quot;.<br /> At its core an exalt's power is undeniable, no need to work for it.<br /> <br /> Fate itself is a bit misunderstood, but on the player end it is an effective prediction and tracking tool (until essence factors in, then it's all bogus) and a way to nudge the odds in your favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T14:41:11-08:00","id":3769,"title":"","content":"Hm. That is interesting. What happens when a Ronin comes into being? Can they be reconected with Fate and the Loom if they are found out by the Sidereals or Pattern Spiders?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/784-durabys","name":"Durabys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T15:25:55-08:00","id":3799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Durabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=3769#post3769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. That is interesting. What happens when a Ronin comes into being? Can they be reconected with Fate and the Loom if they are found out by the Sidereals or Pattern Spiders?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're already connected to Fate and the Loom.<br /> <br /> They just don't work for Heaven and don't receive any training on how to use Astrology. They need to figure it out on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T15:33:25-08:00","id":3802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=3799#post3799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're already connected to Fate and the Loom.<br /> <br /> They just don't work for Heaven and don't receive any training on how to use Astrology. They need to figure it out on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So it is not possible to search for Ronin, get them to Heaven and get a teacher for them, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/784-durabys","name":"Durabys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T15:42:52-08:00","id":3810,"title":"","content":"It is totally possible to hunt down Ronin and bring them in and train them.<br /> There is nothing metaphysically special about Ronin, they just don't <b>currently </b>have access to the loom physically or the basic training to fully understand their powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Do not meddle in the affairs of dragons, for you are crunchy and taste good with ketchup.","edited":{"userid":608,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/608-yoshar","user":"Yoshar","date":". 11-05-2013, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/608-yoshar","name":"Yoshar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T16:52:54-08:00","id":3865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Durabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=3802#post3802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So it is not possible to search for Ronin, get them to Heaven and get a teacher for them, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, it's <i>totally</i> possible to hunt down a Ronin, beat them unconscious, and drag them up to Heaven to chain to a desk and get them to start filing paperwork and playing gofer for another Sid while being rewarded with the occasional bits of esoteric wisdom on beating a man to death with their own spine(aka, having a teacher).<br /> <br /> Ronin are at the end of the day, Sidereals who don't work for Heaven. They're still Exalted, they're still capable of everything a regular Sid can do, they just don't have a job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T16:55:09-08:00","id":3866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=3865#post3865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, it's <i>totally</i> possible to hunt down a Ronin, beat them unconscious, and drag them up to Heaven to chain to a desk and get them to start filing paperwork and playing gofer for another Sid while being rewarded with the occasional bits of esoteric wisdom on beating a man to death with their own spine(aka, having a teacher).<br /> <br /> Ronin are at the end of the day, Sidereals who don't work for Heaven. They're still Exalted, they're still capable of everything a regular Sid can do, they just don't have a job.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Sidereals not working for Heaven isn't an option. They will be found and forcibly persuaded to work because sidereals need more staff. They always need more staff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T19:04:56-08:00","id":3932,"title":"","content":"Hint hint: you don't get on bad terms with the godling that will fill parperwork for you. Even if you are a godling yourself. It's a terrible life choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T19:15:13-08:00","id":3938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=3866#post3866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Sidereals not working for Heaven isn't an option. They will be found and forcibly persuaded to work because sidereals need more staff. They always need more staff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> <br /> For Abyssals, working for the Deathlords is an option even though they always need more Deathknights.<br /> <br /> For Infernals, working for the Yozi and their Third Circles is an option, even though they always need powerful troubleshooters.<br /> <br /> For Dragonblooded, working for the Realm or Lookshy or whatever is an option, even though they always need more Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> For Lunars, working for the Elders of the Silver Pact is an option, even though they always need disposable youngsters to throw at the Realm.<br /> <br /> Solars, of course, do what they want except where mindrape and daiklaves are applied.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals are the only splat that can't really tell their boss where to shove it, but even then, they can pop over to another Nation or else go Apostate(although Modern Alchemicals are perfectly capable of fucking off to do their own thing).<br /> <br /> So if every other splat in the game have &quot;Don't work for their bosses&quot; as an option, I see absolutely no reason why Sidereals should be the only ones that don't have that.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be easy, mind, but nor should it be impossible or a &quot;You've gotta jump through 'Fix Creation' sized hoops to pull it off&quot; task.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T19:50:03-08:00","id":3959,"title":"","content":"Sidereals specifically work for the Bureau of Destiny. They are forced to work there. They get paid but the ones who don't get hunted. Because maintaining fate isn't an easy job. It requires as many sidereals as possible. It's not impossible for a sidereal to hide from them. However, they aren't going to get off like Dragon-Blooded, Lunars, and Solars. Abyssals, Infernals, Alchemicals, and Sidereals gain a shitload of baggage for doing so. Dragon-blooded who join the realm's enemies are in the same position as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:06:22-08:00","id":3982,"title":"","content":"I think there's a sort of misunderstanding about what ronin are here, also a misunderstanding about what Sidereals are and why they work for the Bureau of Destiny.<br /> <br /> Most Sidereals work for the Bureau of Destiny because they want to work for the Bureau of Destiny, because they're found when they're babies and carefully raised, not in Heaven, but in Creation communities with lives and childhoods managed by divine and Sidereal minders who work behind the scenes, <i>Truman Show</i> style, to ensure that the child grows up with the sort of upbringing that will forge them into the sort of people who want to work for the Bureau of Destiny. This is not, precisely, evil -- it's a job that needs doing, and it comes with fantastic rewards, and also Sidereals suffer from the Arcane Fate which means that only other Sidereals and high-Essence gods will ever be able to be proper peers. When they finally come of age and realize that everything in their life up until that moment has lead up to their Exaltation and the beginning of their great work, a reaction like &quot;Oh my god you've been manipulating me to be complicit in your evil schemes this whole time, <i>my entire life has been a lie!&quot;</i> is <b>very uncommon.</b> What mostly happens is they get that hero moment where they realize that they're the heroes of destiny and their patrons have been watching over them and ensuring they learn the right lessons, and now they're finally ready to assume the awesome responsibility of protecting the world. It's like something out of a fantasy book or story where the predestined hero realizes he's the chosen one. (That this position comes with a mansion in Heaven and access to <i>the best</i> food and prostitutes doesn't make the decision to embrace their new roles harder).<br /> <br /> Ronin aren't Sidereals who aren't found when they're babies. I mean, that's probably happened! A couple of times! I'm going to say, oh, a dozen times in the history of Creation, and at least half of those were in the wake of the Usurpation. There are probably five-hundred or a thousand-year stretches in Creation's history where there are absolutely no ronin like that is alive.<br /> <br /> Most ronin are Sidereals who have left the Bureau for personal reasons, grown disillusioned with Heavenly politics, abandoned the patronage of their, uh, patrons, and gone into Creation to find their own way.<br /> <br /> To be clear the Bureau of Destiny is not Treadstone or Blackbriar and ronin Sidereals are not Jason Bourne. They're not hunted like fugitives except for the ones who actually do go ronin because they're fugitives. The Fivescore Fellowship is a tightly-knit peer group, because they all work together and they all suffer the Arcane Fate, so they can't have meaningful, lasting relationships outside of each other. If a family member leaves, reactions are mixed -- some relatives will turn their back, some will hope they return, some will respect their decision, some will try to convince them they're wrong, some will maintain covert ties while pretending to be just as alienated as the rest of the family. Many Sidereals who go ronin <i>come back on their own</i>, eventually. Ten years, fifty years, they find themselves, or they accomplish what they set out to do, or they realize they were wrong, or they just get lonely; they establish ties again and report back to work. That this is a thing that happens is taken into account when the Fellowship decides how to react to a new Sidereal going ronin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:13:52-08:00","id":3992,"title":"","content":"This seems to be a thing then that changed from first and second edition in which they were explicitly brought back into the fold or killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:18:16-08:00","id":3995,"title":"","content":"I don't know about 1st Edition but I own the 2nd Edition Sidereal book and while Ronin aren't exactly the most popular guests at the party they also aren't viciously tracked down and beaten into submission. Creation is big, has big problems and there are only 100 Sidereals at most at a given time. They have better things to do than to try and force an Exalt to do something he or she doesn't want to (good luck with that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/750-shagamemnon","name":"Shagamemnon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:23:26-08:00","id":4000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=3992#post3992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems to be a thing then that changed from first and second edition in which they were explicitly brought back into the fold or killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's because Second Edition was written on the assumption that every social group in the setting was at every other social group's throat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:26:11-08:00","id":4001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4000#post4000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that's because Second Edition was written on the assumption that every social group in the setting was at every other social group's throat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understandable. I guess my point is I was just working with current knowledge. That you can just leave now isn't such a big deal. Though, what happens if they decide to take their ball and go home?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:33:36-08:00","id":4009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4001#post4001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Understandable. I guess my point is I was just working with current knowledge. That you can just leave now isn't such a big deal. Though, what happens if they decide to take their ball and go home?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals are strongly incentivized <i>not</i> to do this for a number of reasons. They're abandoning duties after having been raised from birth to value duty; they're abandoning luxuries undreampt-of by the majority of mankind to live in dirt and squalor in Creation; they're abandoning the only peer group in existence who can truly know and understand them. The Bureau of Destiny and the Five-Score Fellowship have seen Sidereals go ronin before, and they know the danger signs; if at all possible, Sidereals judged to be in danger of going ronin in the near future are afforded lighter duties, other Sidereals try to figure out what's going wrong and address the problem; if times are tough they're reminded that times are tough and everyone is counting on them and they'll be letting everyone down by leaving. Even the Gold/Bronze divide, to some extent, helps prevent Sidereals from going ronin -- this isn't the intent of the split, but Ayesha Ura can always tell her Gold Faction ronin candidate &quot;If you leave now that just gives more ground to Chejop&quot; as a discouragement tactic.<br /> <br /> Nobody decides to take their ball and go home over a minor issue. Each ronin's circumstances is unique and unusual; there is absolutely nothing you can say about what happens when one leaves that applies to all of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:37:49-08:00","id":4013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4009#post4009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sidereals are strongly incentivized <i>not</i> to do this for a number of reasons. They're abandoning duties after having been raised from birth to value duty; they're abandoning luxuries undreampt-of by the majority of mankind to live in dirt and squalor in Creation; they're abandoning the only peer group in existence who can truly know and understand them. The Bureau of Destiny and the Five-Score Fellowship have seen Sidereals go ronin before, and they know the danger signs; if at all possible, Sidereals judged to be in danger of going ronin in the near future are afforded lighter duties, other Sidereals try to figure out what's going wrong and address the problem; if times are tough they're reminded that times are tough and everyone is counting on them and they'll be letting everyone down by leaving. Even the Gold/Bronze divide, to some extent, helps prevent Sidereals from going ronin -- this isn't the intent of the split, but Ayesha Ura can always tell her Gold Faction ronin candidate &quot;If you leave now that just gives more ground to Chejop&quot; as a discouragement tactic.<br /> <br /> Nobody decides to take their ball and go home over a minor issue. Each ronin's circumstances is unique and unusual; there is absolutely nothing you can say about what happens when one leaves that applies to all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm referring to a situation that would cause them all to abandon their duty. In a situation like that what would actually happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:39:29-08:00","id":4014,"title":"","content":"(And it's not always a 100% thing -- there's always those guys who are effectively ronin except they have the one or two other Sidereals who they'll still talk to, and who they maybe do favors for now and again because they know how important it is. You can always do the story about the one cop who retired because he couldn't take the pressure of the job anymore, except his best friend is still on the force and calls him back to consult on the latest serial killer case because it's just horrible and the retired cop is the only guy who was ever good enough to catch 'em when they're this bad.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:44:18-08:00","id":4021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4013#post4013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm referring to a situation that would cause them all to abandon their duty. In a situation like that what would actually happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>All Sidereals abandoning their duties all at once would be so out of character and require such unique circumstances that I wouldn't even begin to guess at the effects unless I knew what those circumstances were. That question is just bizarre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:54:26-08:00","id":4029,"title":"","content":"I just hope the Gold and Bronze Factions have evolved away from being Sidereal only cliques into more major groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:54:36-08:00","id":4030,"title":"","content":"Let's not also forget that Sidereals have the option of taking Sabbaticals, which will hopefully allow them to address whatever issues may be bugging them. But having the uncharacteristic &quot;My life is a lie!&quot; reaction, and/or being moved to abandon heavenly duties and rewards to muddle about in lowly Creation for some powerful reason sounds like acceptable motivations for PCs, who are supposed to stand somewhat outside the norm of their splat!<br /> <br /> Also, I don't recall which book this is mentioned in, but it was stated that the Maidens sometimes &quot;assist&quot; a newborn Sidereal in staying undiscovered because they foresee some need for an autonomous agent with &quot;plausible deniability&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:02:46-08:00","id":4033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4001#post4001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Understandable. I guess my point is I was just working with current knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, I don't think you were. Shagamemnon at the top of the page is right. I just checked every instance of &quot;Ronin&quot; in the 2e Sidereals book: what few places even mention them don't imply that getting hunted down is something that happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:04:24-08:00","id":4036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=3732#post3732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking in generalities, you probably won't see an entity who has &quot;flip off all of an Exalted's cool stuff by remote control&quot; among their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, even if it makes sense that she should be able to do so. This is one thing I've always disliked about Paradox, that it relies on the annoyance of Gods that the Sids are supposed to be working with. One vector of it is even called &quot;Dead Wife Venom&quot;! How am I supposed to get along with these things that callously murdered my mortal husband and/or child?! What's even more galling is that the whole thing is presented as unnecessary. Adjusting Fate isn't harmful to the Loom or painful to the Spiders, it just <i>irritates</i> them...that's all! But they're essentially machines who have to work all the time anyway...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hmm. Can I use my Spirit influencing Charms on Pattern Spiders? Nothing says they're immune...<br /> <br /> I know that punishment mechanics work similarly for other splats, but the Neverborn/Yozi are *supposed* to be antagonistic dicks! I would like Paradox much better if it were an impersonal, automatic reaction from the Loom itself, one which the Spiders actually <i>mitigate, </i>somewhat, so that the Sids are actually indebted to them. Maybe tie it in with the Great Curse, have the Loom react that way because the GC is interfering with the Sid's innate connection to the Loom or something...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:05:06-08:00","id":4037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=3982#post3982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ronin aren't Sidereals who aren't found when they're babies. I mean, that's probably happened! A couple of times! I'm going to say, oh, a dozen times in the history of Creation, and at least half of those were in the wake of the Usurpation. There are probably five-hundred or a thousand-year stretches in Creation's history where there are absolutely no ronin like that is alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, this isn't just a commentary on ronin, right? You're saying that, in general, the chances of someone who inherits the Sidereal fire <i>not</i> being scooped up by the Bureau early in life have always been miniscule and continue to be so in the Time of Tumult?<br /> <br /> I mean, I can believe that. It just that the impression I'd somehow obtained was, essentially, that after five years of Creation being in a &quot;huge deviation from S.O.P&quot; state, and the accompanying increase in non-Fated Sidereal deaths, there were significantly more new Sidereals who were only found by the Bureau in the neighborhood of &quot;months-weeks before Exaltation&quot;, so this data is... requiring some readjustment on my part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\" target=\"_blank\">To the extent possible under law, I hereby waive all copyright and related or neighboring rights to this post.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/666-eco-mono","name":"Eco-Mono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar666_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:09:34-08:00","id":4040,"title":"","content":"I hope the Sidereals book will explore ronin. I don't want to have to hunt down Lea's post every time (awesome though it is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/210-siven","name":"Siven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:09:57-08:00","id":4041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eco-Mono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4037#post4037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this isn't just a commentary on ronin, right? You're saying that, in general, the chances of someone who inherits the Sidereal fire <i>not</i> being scooped up by the Bureau early in life have always been miniscule and continue to be so in the Time of Tumult?<br /> <br /> I mean, I can believe that. It just that the impression I'd somehow obtained was, essentially, that after five years of Creation being in a &quot;huge deviation from S.O.P&quot; state, and the accompanying increase in non-Fated Sidereal deaths, there were significantly more new Sidereals who were only found by the Bureau in the neighborhood of &quot;months-weeks before Exaltation&quot;, so this data is... requiring some readjustment on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like something that might have showed up in a 2e book written by someone trying to increase setting tension and generally contribute to the Thousand Dooms problem, yeah.<br /> <br /> Thing is, I can't imagine any version of the Fivescore Fellowship that doesn't make &quot;Training up the replacement after we lose a guy&quot; their absolute highest priority barring actual apocalypse -- not just potential apocalypse, but &quot;We can find the kid or we can win the boss fight against Cthulhu that's raging right now.&quot; It just won't fit into my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:16:38-08:00","id":4043,"title":"","content":"Addendum: Seriously, saying that because things are hectic lately, the Fivescore Fellowship have been losing track of newborn Sidereals is a bit like that 2e comic in MoEP: DB that demonstrates the devastation of the Great Contagion (which killed 90% of <i>everything</i>) by having a dude complain that no one's willing to buy his slightly withered radishes. Come <i>on.</i> How often is there even <i>a</i> newborn Sidereal? Normally like twice a century, maybe? Less often than that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:18:52-08:00","id":4045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4041#post4041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like something that might have showed up in a 2e book written by someone trying to increase setting tension and generally contribute to the Thousand Dooms problem, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also possible that it was something that I picked up by way of fandom telephone. I think it was over a year between when I got interested in Sids and when I actually obtained the MoEP, and I seem to recall having problems actually finding information in there on what a Sidereal's training is like (other than the flavor text on Savant and the general statement that it's Bronze propaganda heavy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\" target=\"_blank\">To the extent possible under law, I hereby waive all copyright and related or neighboring rights to this post.</a>","edited":{"userid":666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/666-eco-mono","user":"Eco-Mono","date":". 11-06-2013, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/666-eco-mono","name":"Eco-Mono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar666_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:22:32-08:00","id":4049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eco-Mono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4045#post4045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also possible that it was something that I picked up by way of fandom telephone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be!<br /> <br /> It really wouldn't surprise me if it was published, though, but even if it was it needs ignoring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:35:16-08:00","id":4060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4036#post4036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one thing I've always disliked about Paradox, that it relies on the annoyance of Gods that the Sids are supposed to be working with. One vector of it is even called &quot;Dead Wife Venom&quot;! How am I supposed to get along with these things that callously murdered my mortal husband and/or child?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the things that just randomly remove your character from play for a random amount of time, or just randomly kill you. For using the powers that your patronesses empowered you to use on their behalf.<br /> <br /> If Paradox isn't the absolute worst mechanic ever printed in an Exalted rule book, it's at least in the top three.<br /> <br /> And rather than going on a spitting rant re: the ronin discussion, laced with things like how Sidereals hunting down and/or killing ronin only makes any goddamn sense whatsoever if you assume that Sidereals are goddamned idiots who wear their pants on their head and hats on their feet (though a lot of the material written about them probably does give that impression), I think I'm just going to link this page on the old boards.<br /> <br /> Edit: And apparently inserting a link puts it at the bottom of the post on these boards.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T23:04:40-08:00","id":4092,"title":"","content":"This is a <a href=\"http://www.penny-arcade.com\" target=\"_blank\">test</a>. Does this work?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yes it does. Looks like you can insert a link into the middle of a post by making one of the words in the post the link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T23:10:19-08:00","id":4096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4060#post4060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And rather than going on a spitting rant re: the ronin discussion, laced with things like how Sidereals hunting down and/or killing ronin only makes any goddamn sense whatsoever if you assume that Sidereals are goddamned idiots who wear their pants on their head and hats on their feet (though a lot of the material written about them probably does give that impression), I think I'm just going to link this page on the old boards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. What did I just read. 3rd ed Sids book can't come soon enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/210-siven","name":"Siven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T00:03:43-08:00","id":4122,"title":"","content":"Uh oh. Thanks. Finally. I would like to ask how a Ronin comes into being. I heard very strange stories about Ronin's being outside fate because his/her shard went rogue and instead of waiting on its fated host it chose some schmuck on the street or other such non-sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/784-durabys","user":"Durabys","date":". 11-06-2013, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/784-durabys","name":"Durabys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T00:05:59-08:00","id":4124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4036#post4036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, even if it makes sense that she should be able to do so. This is one thing I've always disliked about Paradox, that it relies on the annoyance of Gods that the Sids are supposed to be working with. One vector of it is even called &quot;Dead Wife Venom&quot;! How am I supposed to get along with these things that callously murdered my mortal husband and/or child?! What's even more galling is that the whole thing is presented as unnecessary. Adjusting Fate isn't harmful to the Loom or painful to the Spiders, it just <i>irritates</i> them...that's all! But they're essentially machines who have to work all the time anyway...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hmm. Can I use my Spirit influencing Charms on Pattern Spiders? Nothing says they're immune...<br /> <br /> I know that punishment mechanics work similarly for other splats, but the Neverborn/Yozi are *supposed* to be antagonistic dicks! I would like Paradox much better if it were an impersonal, automatic reaction from the Loom itself, one which the Spiders actually <i>mitigate, </i>somewhat, so that the Sids are actually indebted to them. Maybe tie it in with the Great Curse, have the Loom react that way because the GC is interfering with the Sid's innate connection to the Loom or something...</div> </div> </div> </div>With both the Yozi/Deathlord have their kill switch remote control taken away in 3rd, the Spider ability to fuck you over will probably be toned down to I hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T00:45:59-08:00","id":4140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Durabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4122#post4122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh oh. Thanks. Finally. I would like to ask how a Ronin comes into being. I heard very strange stories about Ronin's being outside fate because his{her shard went rogue and instead of waiting on its fated host it chose some schmuck on the street or other such non-sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, so you have this Sidereal. For one reason or another they choose to stop/never start working for the Bereau of Destiny. Sidereals who make this choice are called Ronin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/613-vegetalss4","name":"Vegetalss4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar613_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T04:52:36-08:00","id":4213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4092#post4092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a <a href=\"http://www.penny-arcade.com\" target=\"_blank\">test</a>. Does this work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, <a href=\"http://www.penny-arcade.com/comic\" target=\"_blank\">further test.</a><br /> <br /> Okay, it seems if you use the URL code or the link button in the advanced editor, it makes the text a link, but if you use the &quot;post a link&quot; button on the left, it adds it to the bottom. That's a tad silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Siven</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. What did I just read. 3rd ed Sids book can't come soon enough</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for the most part, that's a good thread. There was just that point in the middle where some people apparently decided that a line about conflicts between ronin and Bureau Sids meant &quot;SIDEREAL MURDER SQUADS.&quot;<br /> <br /> That or people just really do see the Sidereals as Al Gore's Vice Presidential Action Rangers; &quot;Murder isn't working and it's all we're good at!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T05:39:05-08:00","id":4230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Durabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4122#post4122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh oh. Thanks. Finally. I would like to ask how a Ronin comes into being. I heard very strange stories about Ronin's being outside fate because his{her shard went rogue and instead of waiting on its fated host it chose some schmuck on the street or other such non-sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ronin are Sidereals who go AWOL. Just imagine the Cartman &quot;Screw You Guys, I'm Going Home&quot; clip playing over and over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:56:29-08:00","id":4375,"title":"","content":"Concerning Asna Firstborn:<br /> <br /> I have something of an impression that, while there are Sidereal Charms that interact directly with the Loom of Fate, that they might be deemphasizing the idea that their overall Charmset functions <i>because</i> of the Loom of Fate, such that it wouldn't exactly make sense for being disconnected from it to mess with their Charms, or their Astrology.<br /> <br /> I'd say they can probably still avail of their own magic to connect or reconnect something to Fate, if they need it (probably contested against the strength of an effect that forcefully disconnects them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T10:11:31-08:00","id":4438,"title":"","content":"No mere God can manage such a thing. Nevertheless, I'd say Asna is one of those gods the Sids go out of their way to be cordial with and the same goes with Asna towards the Sids. An oasis of genuine professionalism in a raging sandstorm of goddamn Office Politics and rampant corruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T10:18:28-08:00","id":4447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4438#post4438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No mere God can manage such a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's a &quot;mere&quot; god? Gods run a full gamut, and Asna is supposed to be pretty high up there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T11:39:06-08:00","id":4492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vegetalss4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4140#post4140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, so you have this Sidereal. For one reason or another they choose to stop/never start working for the Bereau of Destiny. Sidereals who make this choice are called Ronin</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I misworded it.So. Again. What happens if somebody who was not fated to become a Sidereal..Exalts as an Sidereal due to somebody screwing up with the Loom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/784-durabys","name":"Durabys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T11:59:17-08:00","id":4499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Durabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4492#post4492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I misworded it.So. Again. What happens if somebody who was not fated to become a Sidereal..Exalts as an Sidereal due to somebody screwing up with the Loom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals gain their Exaltation from birth. It's there, in them, from birth. Some time during puberty it activates and they Exalt. Your question doesn't quite make sense.<br /> <br /> There's some 2e material that contradicts this, but it's written more from a place of &quot;I am writing whatever I want to emphasize that STs can do whatever they want,&quot; not from a place of &quot;Things should make sense.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T12:01:15-08:00","id":4502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Durabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4492#post4492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I misworded it.So. Again. What happens if somebody who was not fated to become a Sidereal..Exalts as an Sidereal due to somebody screwing up with the Loom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't happen. You Exalt as a Sidereal because you were fated to Exalt as a Sidereal. It is your destiny to be a Sidereal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T12:03:01-08:00","id":4503,"title":"","content":"Well.<br /> <br /> It can happen. Because the ST can do whatever he or she wants. But if it does, it's up to the ST to decide how it happens and what that means, because the setting isn't designed on the assumption that it ever does happen and isn't written in such a way that you can go &quot;Okay, if this does happen, it would make sense for this, and this, and this to happen next.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:35:30-08:00","id":4661,"title":"","content":"The impression I got was that only Sidereal inheritors that exalted after an expected death could be trained and shaped in that way. But since so many Sidereal deaths were unexpected (Killed by beings outside fate, killed in the Caul, death by Lunar, etc.), quite a few Sidereals were not predetermined exaltations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/244-seagull","name":"Seagull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar244_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:38:09-08:00","id":4662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seagull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4661#post4661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The impression I got was that only Sidereal inheritors that exalted after an expected death could be trained and shaped in that way. But since so many Sidereal deaths were unexpected (Killed by beings outside fate, killed in the Caul, death by Lunar, etc.), quite a few Sidereals were not predetermined exaltations.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes no sense because it seems to me that far, far more Sidereals must die unexpectedly than expectedly, so if all unexpected Sidereal deaths lead to surprise Exaltations, <i>why</i> does the material <i>only</i> discuss how Sidereals are raised after their predecessors die expectedly? Why devote all that space to the weird exception without calling it an exception or mentioning the norm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:42:49-08:00","id":4667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4375#post4375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning Asna Firstborn:<br /> <br /> I have something of an impression that, while there are Sidereal Charms that interact directly with the Loom of Fate, that they might be deemphasizing the idea that their overall Charmset functions <i>because</i> of the Loom of Fate, such that it wouldn't exactly make sense for being disconnected from it to mess with their Charms, or their Astrology.<br /> <br /> I'd say they can probably still avail of their own magic to connect or reconnect something to Fate, if they need it (probably contested against the strength of an effect that forcefully disconnects them).</div> </div> </div> </div>No charm directly interacts with the loom where changing your status to outside of fate would effect it (Remember celestial battle armor has this option) you lose the ability to be effected by Sidereal charms that effect willpower or influence and astrology doesn't work on you. You'd have the ability to use astrology you just couldn't plly it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:43:08-08:00","id":4668,"title":"","content":"Going just by the 2e Sidereals book, the fluff chapters seemed to say that they trained and groomed projected Sidereals when they could, but when there was an unexpected death they just tried to predict where it would go and lock it down in real time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/244-seagull","name":"Seagull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar244_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:49:10-08:00","id":4673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seagull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4668#post4668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going just by the 2e Sidereals book, the fluff chapters seemed to say that they trained and groomed projected Sidereals when they could, but when there was an unexpected death they just tried to predict where it would go and lock it down in real time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just don't go by what the 2e book says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:55:10-08:00","id":4680,"title":"","content":"I believe scroll of heroes chapter seven (really the only non-problematic chapter in that book) goes into detail on how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:59:56-08:00","id":4684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4662#post4662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes no sense because it seems to me that far, far more Sidereals must die unexpectedly than expectedly, so if all unexpected Sidereal deaths lead to surprise Exaltations, <i>why</i> does the material <i>only</i> discuss how Sidereals are raised after their predecessors die expectedly? Why devote all that space to the weird exception without calling it an exception or mentioning the norm?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, causality being what it is, the only option that really makes sense is that after a Sidereal dies, their Exaltation gets &quot;attached&quot; to a newborn (after visiting Lytek, if that's still a thing). The Fivescore Fellowship then tracks down these Sidereal-in-waiting babies and enrolls them in their <i>The Truman Show</i> prep program. In general this probably isn't too hard, and they've got years; earlier is better but Fate will probably conspire to at least set such children on the right path until the Sids show up. The child eventually Exalts when he is old enough and has his heroic moment.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 11-06-2013, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T16:06:54-08:00","id":4687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4684#post4684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, causality being what it is, the only option that really makes sense is that after a Sidereal dies, their Exaltation gets &quot;attached&quot; to a newborn (after visiting Lytek, if that's still a thing). The Fivescore Fellowship then has to find these Sidereal-in-waiting babies to put them through their <i>The Truman Show</i> prep program. The child eventually Exalts when he is old enough and has his heroic moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T16:11:59-08:00","id":4689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4684#post4684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, causality being what it is, the only option that really makes sense is that after a Sidereal dies, their Exaltation gets &quot;attached&quot; to a newborn (after visiting Lytek, if that's still a thing). The Fivescore Fellowship then tracks down these Sidereal-in-waiting babies and enrolls them in their <i>The Truman Show</i> prep program. In general this probably isn't too hard, and they've got years; earlier is better but Fate will probably conspire to at least set such children on the right path until the Sids show up. The child eventually Exalts when he is old enough and has his heroic moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the first edition book, sidereals could physically mess with the loom to attempt to speed this process up. Usually at the cost of both themselves and the would-be sidereal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T16:28:39-08:00","id":4703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4689#post4689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the first edition book, sidereals could physically mess with the loom to attempt to speed this process up. Usually at the cost of both themselves and the would-be sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't first edition book also said that you have to feed the Loom with enough successes at Craft (Fire) every month or it will stop working?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T16:32:37-08:00","id":4705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4703#post4703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't first edition book also said that you have to feed the Loom with enough successes at Craft (Fire) every month or it will stop working?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still valid, in that the Loom requires constant mechanical maintenance and fate requires constant planning. Representing this mechanically is gratuitous, tough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T16:42:13-08:00","id":4711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4705#post4705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's still valid, in that the Loom requires constant mechanical maintenance and fate requires constant planning. Representing this mechanically is gratuitous, tough.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I'm saying is: the Loom is weird man. You can do a lot stuff to it and how it reacts is basically up to ST fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T17:58:13-08:00","id":4751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4447#post4447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's a &quot;mere&quot; god? Gods run a full gamut, and Asna is supposed to be pretty high up there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Asna isn't an Incarnae, and even they (by design) cannot deny their Exalted power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T18:27:48-08:00","id":4770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by