-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T20:02:51-08:00","id":4807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4705#post4705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's still valid, in that the Loom requires constant mechanical maintenance and fate requires constant planning. Representing this mechanically is gratuitous, tough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Mechanical representations are the clearest, least ambiguous means by which the effort and difficulty of a task can be expressed to players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T20:29:56-08:00","id":4823,"title":"","content":"While that may be true as a general rule, &quot;There was a string of bad Craft rolls one day and Creation ceased to be&quot; is far from desirable. The abstraction is enough in this particular instance, much like I would generally avoid describing the exact defenses on the Jade Pleasure Dome if you want no Exalted to have ever broken in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T20:38:40-08:00","id":4830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4807#post4807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Mechanical representations are the clearest, least ambiguous means by which the effort and difficulty of a task can be expressed to players.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's done by thousands of pattern spiders and requires thousands of successes a day. Like it has rules but it's boring but it's unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T20:49:29-08:00","id":4835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4807#post4807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Mechanical representations are the clearest, least ambiguous means by which the effort and difficulty of a task can be expressed to players.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you start using the task-resolution mechanics of a game to represent a process that is totally outside the scope of what that game's mechanical play experience is like\u2014i.e., using the rules for a game of reincarnated god-kings forging their legend to handle the constant maintenance of the underlying substrate of causality that keeps reality holding together conducted by a hive of clockwork god-spiders\u2014you run into issues. It may be the clearest, least ambiguous means of communication, but it's like a clear, unambiguous sentence written in an entirely different language that's strung with enough false cognates to make it <i>seem</i> parseable, without actually being so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T21:12:08-08:00","id":4840,"title":"","content":"Generally, I think it's probably enough to note &quot;The pattern spiders have an array of highly specialized and technical charms that allow them to handle the day to day reweaving of the Loom that ensures that Creation continues to exist.&quot; in their write up and, whenever the subject comes up in a book &quot;the pattern spiders can handle it.&quot;<br /> <br /> You really only need to get into the mechanical abstractions of bulk reality weaving if a) the PCs are expected to do it on a regular basis, b) it's supposed to have a meaningful result if you fail or succeed, and c) it's supposed to be fun.<br /> <br /> Given that it has the potential to cause reality breakdowns, I get that it's meaningful, but I question whether it's fun and whether it should be something Sids are doing regularly. I also think it's the wrong kind of meaningful. &quot;Roll these dice and tell me when you fail&quot; doesn't sound like it could ever be fun to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T21:47:37-08:00","id":4848,"title":"","content":"If PCs aren't supposed to be involved, don't put stats on it. I thought PCs WERE supposed to be involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T22:35:54-08:00","id":4864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4848#post4848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If PCs aren't supposed to be involved, don't put stats on it. I thought PCs WERE supposed to be involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll grant that this is one of those areas where I think it gets complicated, simply because tracking the day to day operation of the Loom is, basically pure drudgery that the PCs shouldn't have to get involved in and thus doesn't need stats (except possibly as a prison sentence), but, searching the Loom, fate planning, fate implementation, and, especially, fate alteration are all things I'd expect PC Sids to get involved with, so there should be some mechanical weight there.<br /> <br /> Still, I'd imagine that would be doable, since that's basically what Astrology was in the previous two editions. Add in some rules for examining the Loom to find out stuff and you're good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T01:00:25-08:00","id":4890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4770#post4770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any god. Compared to the Exalted anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>How positively wretched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T01:08:13-08:00","id":4892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asna isn't an Incarnae, and even they (by design) cannot deny their Exalted power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about denying Exalted power, I'm talking about the implicit assumption that gods are pathetic.<br /> <br /> This idea that there's this enormous, inexorable gulf between the Incarnae and <i>all other gods</i>, to the point that Panoply Charms were basically a massive innovation because Michael Goodwin thought, correctly, that the usual spirit mechanics were insufficient to represent gods as mighty as the Incarnae were assumed to be, is <i>terrible</i>; it does not fit with the setting assumptions about the gods, and it's overall not a good thing to make gods in general seem pathetic because then the Exalted peerage to them lacks credibility.<br /> <br /> This is probably why there aren't universal spirit Charms anymore; maybe Ahlat can finally have a Charmset tailored to how impressive he's supposed to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T01:14:44-08:00","id":4894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought PCs WERE supposed to be involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trick there would seem to be &quot;put stats only on the parts that PCs are involved with&quot;.<br /> <br /> Stats for the general Fate planning that the Conventions that every single Sidereal is supposed to be a part of, and maybe stats to represent how any individual agendas a Sidereal wants to construct need to interact with and account for this planning to avoid errors, that might be all right, but it's different from stating exactly how many successes per day are needed by the pattern spiders to keep Creation intact.<br /> <br /> I mean, have you <i>seen</i> the sidebar in question? It's got to be at least a thousand words long!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T01:52:20-08:00","id":4911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4890#post4890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How positively wretched.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, I do get that it's much more nuanced than this and the results of any conflict between an Exalt and a God depend more on the specific capabilities of the two parties and the nature of the conflict, more than on their merits as Exalted and God.<br /> <br /> That said, I really feel like the statement encapsulates the Exalted very well. The Exalted were empowered by the gods, but the gods wrought better than they knew and created beings superior to them. Even if a given god can outclass a given Exalt, despite their power over humans and the foundations of reality, gods as a whole are lesser beings when compared to the might of the Exalted host. Asserting that you are no mere god should get you in lots of trouble if you actually do it in game, but I feel like the game itself asserts this as part of it's premise (unlike, say, Scion or the WoD where nigh invincible elder beings lording it over you is a common part of the game).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T01:55:05-08:00","id":4912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4892#post4892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not talking about denying Exalted power, I'm talking about the implicit assumption that gods are pathetic.<br /> <br /> This idea that there's this enormous, inexorable gulf between the Incarnae and <i>all other gods</i>, to the point that Panoply Charms were basically a massive innovation because Michael Goodwin thought, correctly, that the usual spirit mechanics were insufficient to represent gods as mighty as the Incarnae were assumed to be, is <i>terrible</i>; it does not fit with the setting assumptions about the gods, and it's overall not a good thing to make gods in general seem pathetic because then the Exalted peerage to them lacks credibility.<br /> <br /> This is probably why there aren't universal spirit Charms anymore; maybe Ahlat can finally have a Charmset tailored to how impressive he's supposed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Ok, this I'll grant. The gods should only be lesser when compared to the Exalted and, even then, there should be Non-Incarne gods out there that any given Exalt wouldn't want to mess with without some careful preparation first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T02:06:01-08:00","id":4916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4911#post4911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exalted were empowered by the gods, but the gods wrought better than they knew and created beings superior to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the Dragon Blooded?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T03:01:53-08:00","id":4936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4916#post4916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about the Dragon Blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://img837.imageshack.us/img837/2096/ywco.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Same thing applies as with other Exalted - while a particular DB can, at the moment at least, be weaker than a god, another can probably kick that god's ass, or the same DB can come back with his Sworn Brotherhood and do just that. Superiority is a complex thing in Exalted, and general statements about it don't always apply to the situation at hand, but overall, the Dragon-Blooded are still gods' superiors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T03:50:48-08:00","id":4939,"title":"","content":"In Creation, making a statement like, &quot;I battled a god and survived,&quot; or &quot;I killed a god,&quot; or &quot;I tricked a god,&quot; should be impressive statements, even for the Exalted, in the general. Since I have also been looking through the 1e core for another thread, here is a quote that encapsulates how I feel Exalted and gods should consider one another:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirits are the least among gods. Where the Celestines are deities of the sky and of time and of living and dying, the little gods are the deities of individual places and things. They are less powerful than their mighty brothers and sisters, weak enough that one of the Exalted --- or even a strong and clever mortal --- can best them. Yet, they are deities nevertheless and not to be trifled with. They manipulate Essence more easily than one of the Exalted, and they are beloved by their greater brothers and sisters. Those who do arm or offense to the little gods risks the implacable wrath of their celestial relatives. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T03:59:22-08:00","id":4942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4936#post4936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same thing applies as with other Exalted - while a particular DB can, at the moment at least, be weaker than a god, another can probably kick that god's ass, or the same DB can come back with his Sworn Brotherhood and do just that. Superiority is a complex thing in Exalted, and general statements about it don't always apply to the situation at hand, but overall, the Dragon-Blooded are still gods' superiors.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? What makes Exalted &quot;the gods' superiors&quot;? How does that account for how gods vary wildly in power? How is the fact that the Dragon Blooded are the weakest of the Exalted in any way meaningful if you just go &quot;they're still stronger than those pissant gods&quot;, especially considering that there are great warriors of the Celestial City? How does any of this play into the fact that Celestial Lions have always been presented as actual relevant security for the gates of Heaven, such that a Solar dueling one of them would be hard put and fighting off a dozen would be extremely difficult to surmount?<br /> <br /> And saying &quot;oh, you can just build up your numbers of Dragon Blooded to overcome the god&quot; is quite the cop out, considering that you can do the same with gods, and there are more of them.<br /> <br /> The idea that gods are patently inferior to the Exalted is not actually present in the written setting, and that the mechanics have generally born it out is a failing of the mechanics. The Incarnae are <i>not</i> supposed to be the only gods who are anything comparable to or above the Exalted (look at descriptions of the divine ranks in Compass: Yu-Shan), whatever shoddy mechanics forced their write-ups to accommodate to actually present their status. This is why we need to get rid of universal god Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T04:15:26-08:00","id":4948,"title":"","content":"Sidereal charm fluff keep going on and on about how the Maiden give them terrifying power over spirits so I don't expect &quot;Asna hate your gut so you can't use this charm and that charm and this other charm&quot; to be a thing in 3rd","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T04:41:59-08:00","id":4957,"title":"","content":"Although I do wonder, if Getimian alchemy is supposed to follow the logic of them having pattern spiders in their meridian lines, and they can construct these kind of contrarian destines with them and infect the Tapestry with them in a way that is bad in general and possibly particularly to Sidereals, what kind of attacks can be launched specifically through the medium of Fate and how might these disrupt the Sidereals in implementing their purpose and the Maidens' designs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T07:33:37-08:00","id":5059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4942#post4942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How? What makes Exalted &quot;the gods' superiors&quot;? How does that account for how gods vary wildly in power? How is the fact that the Dragon Blooded are the weakest of the Exalted in any way meaningful if you just go &quot;they're still stronger than those pissant gods&quot;, especially considering that there are great warriors of the Celestial City? How does any of this play into the fact that Celestial Lions have always been presented as actual relevant security for the gates of Heaven, such that a Solar dueling one of them would be hard put and fighting off a dozen would be extremely difficult to surmount?<br /> <br /> And saying &quot;oh, you can just build up your numbers of Dragon Blooded to overcome the god&quot; is quite the cop out, considering that you can do the same with gods, and there are more of them.<br /> <br /> The idea that gods are patently inferior to the Exalted is not actually present in the written setting, and that the mechanics have generally born it out is a failing of the mechanics. The Incarnae are <i>not</i> supposed to be the only gods who are anything comparable to or above the Exalted (look at descriptions of the divine ranks in Compass: Yu-Shan), whatever shoddy mechanics forced their write-ups to accommodate to actually present their status. This is why we need to get rid of universal god Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a number of gods that should be easy to overcome. I always got the idea that unless you were a rank 4 or 5 ( essence 6+ ) spirit focused in combat if you were going up against a combat focused Celestial Exalt there would be no way to win. To me I always took Celestial Lions as harder in numbers than individuals. When you got into things like Elemental dragons though, that's when you were running up hill. However, someone like Jorst or Ryza (I'm too lazy to get my book out if I'm not spelling the Bureaucracy god's name right.) should still be easy to beat because they aren't remotely focused on combat. Not every god is going to be combat capable. In fact, I'd say most aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T08:16:54-08:00","id":5084,"title":"","content":"Just because you can kill it doesn't make you superior. Someone killed Martin Luther King Jr. Does that make whatever bigot did it superior?<br /> <br /> When the Exalted can do the job of the gods just as well, then perhaps you can make claims of superiority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T08:24:22-08:00","id":5088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=5059#post5059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always got the idea that unless you were a rank 4 or 5 ( essence 6+ ) spirit focused in combat if you were going up against a combat focused Celestial Exalt there would be no way to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given what seems to be implied by the meaning of the Essence curve in the QC preview, I would feel like it might be a bit overkill to make it so that a god needs to be on the higher end of the power scale to be a relevant threat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me I always took Celestial Lions as harder in numbers than individuals. When you got into things like Elemental dragons though, that's when you were running up hill. However, someone like Jorst or Ryza (I'm too lazy to get my book out if I'm not spelling the Bureaucracy god's name right.) should still be easy to beat because they aren't remotely focused on combat. Not every god is going to be combat capable. In fact, I'd say most aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like there are two things to this:<br /> 1) Okay, so a god who isn't very good at fighting won't be much of a challenge in a fight. That says absolutely nothing useful in comparing the might of gods and Exalted.<br /> 2) Let's take the Jorst example; how is Jorst fighting you? Or more importantly, where? Because if it's in the middle of the relevant kind of forest, it seems like he'd be more about getting the trees to swing around at you or uprooting themselves and going crazy, or overall go &quot;last battle in the movie version of Prince Caspian&quot; on you. You know; kind of &quot;wrath of god&quot; stuff? They're not all kung fu fighting.<br /> <br /> I think that's my main problem with the &quot;gods are intrinsically weaker than Exalts&quot; thing; it kind of assumes that they'll be doing the same kinds of stuff.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously there <i>will</i> be kung fu fighting gods (including gods who don't have it naturally as part of their nature but have learned Martial Arts), and it seems like they should be credible challenges to Exalted as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T08:35:14-08:00","id":5093,"title":"","content":"Honestly, for an experienced combat focused Exalt (Considering a group of E5 Solar are supposed to be able to kill the sun unless that model has changed) Gods shouldn't be a challenging direct opponent unless we are dealing with a directional war god or someone else like that. But indirectly specific gods like Jorst should definitely be a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T12:11:22-08:00","id":5292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4957#post4957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I do wonder, if Getimian alchemy is supposed to follow the logic of them having pattern spiders in their meridian lines, and they can construct these kind of contrarian destines with them and infect the Tapestry with them in a way that is bad in general and possibly particularly to Sidereals, what kind of attacks can be launched specifically through the medium of Fate and how might these disrupt the Sidereals in implementing their purpose and the Maidens' designs?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's anything like Snarling Loom Deception, it will allow them to do Sidereal-like things far better and with none of the attendant headaches and stupidity of Sidereals.<br /> <br /> ...I hope it's nothing like Snarling Loom Deception.<br /> <br /> I also hope that the inverse is true. If Getimians can just ooze out Bad Stuff for the Loom/Fate whenever they feel like it, a Sidereal should be able to reverse-fate-hack a Getimian. Having pattern spiders in your body should become a lot less awesome if the guy you just pissed off is one of the 100 Exalts that pattern spiders are hard coded to obey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T12:42:40-08:00","id":5324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=5292#post5292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's anything like Snarling Loom Deception, it will allow them to do Sidereal-like things far better and with none of the attendant headaches and stupidity of Sidereals.<br /> <br /> ...I hope it's nothing like Snarling Loom Deception.<br /> <br /> I also hope that the inverse is true. If Getimians can just ooze out Bad Stuff for the Loom/Fate whenever they feel like it, a Sidereal should be able to reverse-fate-hack a Getimian. Having pattern spiders in your body should become a lot less awesome if the guy you just pissed off is one of the 100 Exalts that pattern spiders are hard coded to obey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, Loom Snarling Deception should have been what Resplendent Destinies were. Don't even get me started on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T08:43:23-08:00","id":6859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4043#post4043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Addendum: Seriously, saying that because things are hectic lately, the Fivescore Fellowship have been losing track of newborn Sidereals is a bit like that 2e comic in MoEP: DB that demonstrates the devastation of the Great Contagion (which killed 90% of <i>everything</i>) by having a dude complain that no one's willing to buy his slightly withered radishes. Come <i>on.</i> How often is there even <i>a</i> newborn Sidereal? Normally like twice a century, maybe? Less often than that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Slightly-withered-radishes-guy is my new hero. Now I picture him in every major event in Creation's history, worrying about how it affects his radishes. Picturing him bringing a cartload of radishes to the Calibration Feast only for it to get knocked over by the fighting DBs and Solars -- &quot;my radishes!&quot;<br /> <br /> When the first Primoridal to fall strikes the earth and becomes a Neverborn, it obliterates a cart of his radishes, and later, we see him angrily petitioning the victorious UCS and Exalted to compensate him for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T09:52:44-08:00","id":6894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=6859#post6859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slightly-withered-radishes-guy is my new hero. Now I picture him in every major event in Creation's history, worrying about how it affects his radishes. Picturing him bringing a cartload of radishes to the Calibration Feast only for it to get knocked over by the fighting DBs and Solars -- &quot;my radishes!&quot;<br /> <br /> When the first Primoridal to fall strikes the earth and becomes a Neverborn, it obliterates a cart of his radishes, and later, we see him angrily petitioning the victorious UCS and Exalted to compensate him for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>His supplications reach the ear of the humblest forbidden god, who sided with the most fecund of the ousted Primordials in the war and succeeded in laying low thereafter.<br /> <br /> Through this god's machinations was born the single illicit Exigent returning from age to age: Exalted and Exalted-hunter both, Chosen of Radishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T11:07:46-08:00","id":6931,"title":"","content":"Oh God what have I done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T11:37:16-08:00","id":6945,"title":"","content":"I still say we need Chejop Kejack and Asna Firstborn to get some time together. The six-armed Starborn would be Creation's first Spidereal Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T11:45:52-08:00","id":6949,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the derail but oh my god! I don't wanna steal your signature, Jen, so please post often ^__^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T12:41:13-08:00","id":6974,"title":"","content":"There need to be a decent number of new Sidereal exalts, surely, otherwise how do you get a group of starting characters for PCs? And it's supposed to be a dangerous job, which a 2/100 chance of dying per century wouldn't really count as..<br /> <br /> I'd also prefer to have a decent amount of variety in Sidereal background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/957-wulfram","name":"Wulfram","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T13:12:19-08:00","id":6995,"title":"","content":"You know, while I get and agree with the point Lea was making, I do think that if the Declaration of the Scarlet Empress is supposed to take place something like a few months after the Balorian Crusade was destroyed, that comic does kind of work less as a depiction of the devastation of the Contagion and more as an instance of how the disaster had passed and life was resuming and what they really needed then was somebody to get the central government going again.<br /> <br /> It... <i>does</i> kind of fit with the picture I got of the post-Crusade per-Declaration environment painted by Exalted: The Dragon Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T02:54:51-08:00","id":8693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=6931#post6931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh God what have I done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine how I feel. Jeez. If I knew this derail would happen I wouldn't have posted my question in the first place. *facepalms HARD*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/784-durabys","name":"Durabys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T04:37:01-08:00","id":9587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Durabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=8693#post8693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine how I feel. Jeez. If I knew this derail would happen I wouldn't have posted my question in the first place. *facepalms HARD*</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi there! Welcome to the Internet, you must be new here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As far as derails go for this board, this is actually fairly minor.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:09:56-08:00","id":9851,"title":"","content":"Yeah this happens. It has happened to almost every thread I made on the other forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1044-veritas1980","name":"Veritas1980","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1044_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":4,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:26:12-08:00","id":9863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=4043#post4043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Addendum: Seriously, saying that because things are hectic lately, the Fivescore Fellowship have been losing track of newborn Sidereals is a bit like that 2e comic in MoEP: DB that demonstrates the devastation of the Great Contagion (which killed 90% of <i>everything</i>) by having a dude complain that no one's willing to buy his slightly withered radishes. Come <i>on.</i> How often is there even <i>a</i> newborn Sidereal? Normally like twice a century, maybe? Less often than that?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a tangent but the Great Contagion going from 90% of humans to 90% of everything was one of the silliest changes in the game line.<br /> It's one thing to say a lot of people died, but 90% of everything means Creation bounced back absurdly fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:45:47-08:00","id":9873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=9863#post9863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a tangent but the Great Contagion going from 90% of humans to 90% of everything was one of the silliest changes in the game line.<br /> It's one thing to say a lot of people died, but 90% of everything means Creation bounced back absurdly fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>You <i>could</i> actually salvage that given the presence of Wood Elementals/Wood Elemental Dragons, but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T13:25:41-08:00","id":9945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=9863#post9863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a tangent but the Great Contagion going from 90% of humans to 90% of everything was one of the silliest changes in the game line.<br /> It's one thing to say a lot of people died, but 90% of everything means Creation bounced back absurdly fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably helped that the ruins were devoured by the Wyld.<br /> <br /> That said, I wonder where that specific detail might have come in.<br /> <br /> All I know is that Grabowski cited it as a reference for why the First Edition Lunar plan wasn't likely to have the same dramatic impact that the Great Contagion did partially because they'd only be killing humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T14:02:20-08:00","id":9969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=9945#post9945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It probably helped that the ruins were devoured by the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that in 2nd edition is that we know where the Contagion started and it's still very much part of Creation.<br /> Though for 3rd edition... that could also be an interesting way to address the problems with the Dowager. What if she lost the Well of Udr in the Balorian Crusade? My god... I wish I'd thought of that sooner, now she's actually got a reason to use Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 11-13-2013, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T14:19:01-08:00","id":9975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=9969#post9969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with that in 2nd edition is that we know where the Contagion started and it's still very much part of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>How big is that shadowland supposed to be?<br /> <br /> How frequent are shadowlands in the East in general? It feels like it would be less amenable to them than elsewhere.<br /> <br /> I mean, if the Contagion was killing Eastern flora and fauna faster than the Pole of Wood could regenerate them, but then the Contagion stopped...<br /> <br /> I'm probably quibbling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if she lost the Well of Udr in the Balorian Crusade? My god... I wish I'd thought of that sooner, now she's actually got a reason to use Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't she?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T15:35:19-08:00","id":10040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=9975#post9975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How big is that shadowland supposed to be?<br /> <br /> How frequent are shadowlands in the East in general? It feels like it would be less amenable to them than elsewhere.<br /> <br /> I mean, if the Contagion was killing Eastern flora and fauna faster than the Pole of Wood could regenerate them, but then the Contagion stopped...</div> </div> </div> </div>Previously the Great Contagion has been depicted as coming directly the Well of Udr.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't she?</div> </div> </div> </div>She's just had the Shoat of the Mire for the last two editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T16:54:28-08:00","id":10081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=10040#post10040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Previously the Great Contagion has been depicted as coming directly the Well of Udr.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, that's why my references to the East and the seemingly unusually large shadowland around it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's just had the Shoat of the Mire for the last two editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah...<br /> <br /> I feel that's less a matter of &quot;here's a good reason to have more Abyssal Exalted&quot; and more &quot;there is no good reason not to have more than one Abyssal Exalted&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though I think the Dowager in general could use a bit more personality; right now all she's got is a halfway interesting design (which has frequently failed to come across well in illustration in my opinion), being credited with the Great Contagion (which honestly feels like it could have been pulled out of a hat), and some weird arbitrary nonsense with orphans and destroyed villages.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T17:27:31-08:00","id":10093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/3710-explain-please-asna-firstborn-the-loom-and-sidereals?p=5088#post5088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given what seems to be implied by the meaning of the Essence curve in the QC preview, I would feel like it might be a bit overkill to make it so that a god needs to be on the higher end of the power scale to be a relevant threat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like there are two things to this:<br /> 1) Okay, so a god who isn't very good at fighting won't be much of a challenge in a fight. That says absolutely nothing useful in comparing the might of gods and Exalted.<br /> 2) Let's take the Jorst example; how is Jorst fighting you? Or more importantly, where? Because if it's in the middle of the relevant kind of forest, it seems like he'd be more about getting the trees to swing around at you or uprooting themselves and going crazy, or overall go &quot;last battle in the movie version of Prince Caspian&quot; on you. You know; kind of &quot;wrath of god&quot; stuff? They're not all kung fu fighting.<br /> <br /> I think that's my main problem with the &quot;gods are intrinsically weaker than Exalts&quot; thing; it kind of assumes that they'll be doing the same kinds of stuff.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously there <i>will</i> be kung fu fighting gods (including gods who don't have it naturally as part of their nature but have learned Martial Arts), and it seems like they should be credible challenges to Exalted as well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know, at no point did I say a God could not beat an Exalt in a fight.<br /> <br /> I just said they don't have the Mojo to deny an Exalt their own Mojo. Which is a good thing, because when you're up against the Entities that can order damn near everything except attacking you, you really really don't want the order to depower them to actually <i>work</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T17:41:00-08:00","id":10100,"title":"","content":"Ahhh, now I see it; you meant &quot;mere&quot; in comparison to the scope of the task under scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T14:18:18-08:00","id":16790,"title":"","content":"I think it was mentioned that people who take too long at their task (I mean when it's a task that should take a week, they've been gone for months) that they do send out some kind of search party to make sure they're alright and to remind them of their duty in heaven.<br /> <br /> My understanding is that after the Empress ditched creation, things got kinda crazy busy for the Sidereals and their control is slipping in a number of ways. I used that to justify my sidereal dude not being known for two years after his exaltation. It was still according to someone's plan, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1148-palemask","name":"Palemask","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}